{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He shall not come for any dead persons.</b> The body [is implied], for מת is a body. The noun is lacking [the word] גוף, and likewise ועשיר יענה עזות (Proverbs 18:23), and מאכלו בריאה — תחסר שה." "The meaning of <b>he shall not come</b>: into a tent or into a house where the dead person is." "The meaning of <b>for his father and for his mother</b>: for it is a commandment upon him to honor them in their lives and in their death — all the more so for his brother and his son."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The final phrase 'תחסר שה' is textually obscure; translated hyper-literally. The prooftext in the middle is from Proverbs 18:23."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:35.545104930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}